4.2 Identification of the Deep Binding Pocket 

Potential ligand-binding pockets were identified using P2Rank 2.5.1. Analysis of the predicted pockets in the context of the three MexB conformational states identified a functionally relevant pocket within the porter domain of the Binding-state structure. This pocket was selected as the Deep Binding Pocket (DBP) for subsequent ligand screening (Radoslav  et al., 2018). 

The docking region was defined around the predicted DBP using a grid center of −11.731, −0.815, and −28.409 Å along the X, Y, and Z axes, respectively. The docking box dimensions were 32 × 28 × 28 Å. 

Six residues located within the selected pocket were defined as the core DBP residues: VAL139, PHE178, TYR327, PHE573, PHE610, and PHE628. 

