4.5 Three-dimensional visualization of the MexB Deep Binding Pocket 

A three-dimensional structural representation was generated to visualize the location of the representative top-ranked ligand CHEMBL254328 within the MexB Binding-state DBP. 

The overall MexB trimer is shown with the Access, Binding, and Extrusion protomers represented separately, while the Binding-state protomer containing the docking site is highlighted. A magnified view of the DBP demonstrates that CHEMBL254328 is positioned within the predicted internal binding cavity and is surrounded by the six predefined core residues (Pettersen et al., 2021). 

The minimum distances between CHEMBL254328 and the six core residues were approximately 3.15–3.73 Å, consistent with the quantitative contact analysis. The visualization therefore provides structural confirmation that the selected ligand occupies the intended DBP region. 

